{"name":"Cranberry","hex":"#9e003a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cranberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A community and neighbourhood in the city of Powell River, British Columbia, Canada.","An unincorporated community in Hazle Township, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cranberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cranberry","blocks":[{"text":"Cranberries are a group of evergreen dwarf shrubs or trailing vines in the subgenus Oxycoccus of the genus Vaccinium. Cranberries are low, creeping shrubs or vines up to 2 meters (7 ft) long and 5 to 20 centimeters in height; they have slender stems that are not thickly woody and have small evergreen leaves. The flowers are dark pink. The fruit is a berry that is larger than the leaves of the plant; it is initially light green, turning red when ripe. The raw berry is edible and has a tart taste due to the low sugar content and high acidity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cranberry_bog.jpg/330px-Cranberry_bog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranberry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cranberries20101210.jpg/500px-Cranberries20101210.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cranberries20101210.jpg/500px-Cranberries20101210.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Raw cranberries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACranberries20101210.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Cranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg/500px-Cranberry_harvest%2C_Kingston_Massachusetts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki